One thing worth flagging: at exactly 1000 bytes the C buffer has no NUL terminator, so [38;5;10mstrchr[0m reads past the array — undefined behavior that can't be translated directly. Rather than guess, I measured it across [38;5;10m-O0[0m/[38;5;10m-O2[0m/[38;5;10m-O3 -fstack-protector-strong[0m and with the stack shifted by a 60 KB environment variable and 500 extra variables. Every build reported [38;5;10mA: 1000[0m, matching what the Rust code does by capping at the array end. The Rust behavior is pinned to that observation and is memory-safe, but it rests on measured UB rather than on guaranteed C semantics.[0m[0m
